["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Mental events obey no laws, and that is how freedom and determinism coexist Davidson answers the mind-body problem with token identity: a mental event and a physical event are the same event, causation requires a covering law, but there are no strict laws under mental descriptions — so determinism and freedom can both hold. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 398: Donald Davidson on Mind vs. Body (Part One) Mind-body problem Reasons and causes Anomalous monism Analytic philosophy Philosophy of mind token-token identity type-type identity anomalous monism nomological supervenience\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-pel-戴维森-理由就是原因-但心理事件无律可循/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/f/d/6/5/fd65c04f68a17a9b16c3140a3186d450/PartiallyExaminedLifeLogo_3000x3000-20260817-srfrcjo9pc.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">52:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>Mental events obey no laws, and that is how freedom and determinism coexist</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Davidson answers the mind-body problem with token identity: a mental event and a physical event are the same event, causation requires a covering law, but there are no strict laws under mental descriptions — so determinism and freedom can both hold.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Mind-body problem</span><span class=\"tag\">Reasons and causes</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"bin Laden Was Not Born Extreme: Three Turns Pushed Him Onto the Jihadist Road bin Laden was not an extremist as a child but a marginal figure in a wealthy Saudi family; three turning points — the 1979 Mecca siege, the Afghan battlefield and the Gulf War — put him on the road to global jihad, and he always wanted to bring down the Saudi royal family more than he wanted to fight the United States alone. Dan Snow&#x27;s History Hit History Hit The Making of Osama bin Laden History of terrorism al-Qaeda bin Laden Middle East politics War on Terror Wahhabi Mujahideen Muslim Brotherhood Tora Bora\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-historyhit-本-拉登的极端化是选择不是宿命/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f67d4b795a40fffd3b2c/1786636082162-9c939840-0417-4daa-8462-7e282931a6db.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Dan Snow&#x27;s History Hit</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>bin Laden Was Not Born Extreme: Three Turns Pushed Him Onto the Jihadist Road</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">bin Laden was not an extremist as a child but a marginal figure in a wealthy Saudi family; three turning points — the 1979 Mecca siege, the Afghan battlefield and the Gulf War — put him on the road to global jihad, and he always wanted to bring down the Saudi royal family more than he wanted to fight the United States alone.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">History of terrorism</span><span class=\"tag\">al-Qaeda</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"China&#x27;s EV industry wasn&#x27;t planned into existence — local credit bought the right of way This episode takes half the credit for the rise of China&#x27;s carmakers away from central industrial policy: the real engine was local governments trading loans and equity for factories, and entrepreneurs using relationships to route around SOE licensing — at the cost of an overcapacity nobody can now unwind. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk The Rise of China’s Electric Vehicle Industry EVs Local government Industrial policy Overcapacity Exports SOE reform three bigs and three smalls township and village enterprise (TVE) 10 city thousand vehicle project Hefei model special purpose vehicle (SPV)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-chinatalk-中国电动车不是北京规划出来的-是地方政府用信贷买路权买出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/d33ffece-99d8-11f1-8cc6-f328fc037173/image/b16c651d8b1a202e90a15ea6dc470b88.jpeg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:54:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>China&#x27;s EV industry wasn&#x27;t planned into existence — local credit bought the right of way</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">This episode takes half the credit for the rise of China&#x27;s carmakers away from central industrial policy: the real engine was local governments trading loans and equity for factories, and entrepreneurs using relationships to route around SOE licensing — at the cost of an overcapacity nobody can now unwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">EVs</span><span class=\"tag\">Local government</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"When a child asks permission for everything, the problem is perfectionism, not the child A four-and-a-half-year-old boy comes home from preschool and starts asking permission for everything; his mother finds that when she sets perfectionism aside and stops handing him answers, his ability to solve problems on his own far exceeds what she expected. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Re-release: Creative Problem-Solving (Without Giving the Answer) Interest-led learning Perfectionism Scaffolding questions Metacognition Nature school lantern consciousness yes space learning exploration scaffolding metacognition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-parentmojo-孩子不需要你给出答案-只需要一个脚手架/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://artwork.captivate.fm/12802a36-dbca-4912-a62e-cbce5aacddb8/podcast-cover-your-parenting-mojo-03-01-copy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">54:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>When a child asks permission for everything, the problem is perfectionism, not the child</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A four-and-a-half-year-old boy comes home from preschool and starts asking permission for everything; his mother finds that when she sets perfectionism aside and stops handing him answers, his ability to solve problems on his own far exceeds what she expected.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Interest-led learning</span><span class=\"tag\">Perfectionism</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Troubles were not a religious war but demographic anxiety and zero-sum politics For decades Britain ignored the demographic anxiety and economic imbalance inside Northern Ireland and left the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, the violence in Ulster was about to run out of control. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 697. The Troubles: Murder in Belfast (Part 1) The Troubles British politics Nationalism Sectarian conflict The 1960s Paisley The Troubles\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-restishistory-北爱冲突不是宗教战争-而是人口与经济的零和博弈/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/00c0a118-2426-11ee-b258-73d331d0123b/image/db3295fcd9d3a7113e8000e931f0541d.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:26:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>The Troubles were not a religious war but demographic anxiety and zero-sum politics</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">For decades Britain ignored the demographic anxiety and economic imbalance inside Northern Ireland and left the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, the violence in Ulster was about to run out of control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">The Troubles</span><span class=\"tag\">British politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers Between Fabs: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity TSMC exploits the more than 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck half-processed wafers from its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity while N5 converts to N3. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks. Asianometry Asianometry How TSMC Uses Old Fabs to Make New Chips TSMC Chip capacity Advanced packaging AI compute Semiconductor manufacturing Cross-node utilization cross-node utilization gate-all-around (GAA) back end of the line (BEOL) CoWoS FOUP\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-asianometry-台积电用货车把旧厂改造成-ai-新产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/cDxVYQrxeiQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">15:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers Between Fabs: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">TSMC exploits the more than 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck half-processed wafers from its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity while N5 converts to N3. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">TSMC</span><span class=\"tag\">Chip capacity</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Anti-vaccine sentiment is not new: Jenner&#x27;s own book is full of people cursing him This episode shows the anti-vaccine movement is as old as vaccines themselves; phage SPO1 uses liquid-liquid phase-separated condensates to switch transcriptional phases; ancient smallpox DNA from South America confirms transmission by European colonization; and declining reading plus AI-generated content threaten our powers of discernment. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1349: Smallpox and mummies Phage Vaccines Smallpox Phase separation Anti-vaccine Transcriptional regulation liquid-liquid phase separation (LLPS) intrinsically disordered region (IDR) biomolecular condensate RNA polymerase holoenzyme vaccinia virus factory synonymous substitution rate\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-twiv-反疫苗古已有之-噬菌体凝聚体是转录调控核心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">2:03:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>Anti-vaccine sentiment is not new: Jenner&#x27;s own book is full of people cursing him</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">This episode shows the anti-vaccine movement is as old as vaccines themselves; phage SPO1 uses liquid-liquid phase-separated condensates to switch transcriptional phases; ancient smallpox DNA from South America confirms transmission by European colonization; and declining reading plus AI-generated content threaten our powers of discernment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Vaccines</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Roman Empire ran on enslaved people, not on its legions Rome&#x27;s administration, its army, its domestic work, its workshops and its mines ran almost entirely on enslaved people; after Carthage fell in 146 BC slavery became the engine of the economy, and once Augustus stopped expanding, that population reproduced itself by birth. The Ancients The Ancients How Slavery Built the Roman Empire Roman history Slavery Roman Empire Ancient economy Gender and class manumission verna servus poenae dispensator freedmen Pax Romana\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-ancients-罗马帝国是奴隶制的产物-无奴隶则无帝国/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f9e74b795a6299fd3b58/1786707577519-4bb3c814-5c68-4332-b80a-e32efec0a891.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>The Roman Empire ran on enslaved people, not on its legions</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Rome&#x27;s administration, its army, its domestic work, its workshops and its mines ran almost entirely on enslaved people; after Carthage fell in 146 BC slavery became the engine of the economy, and once Augustus stopped expanding, that population reproduced itself by birth.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Roman history</span><span class=\"tag\">Slavery</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"America Rescued the Yen for Its Own Trillion in Treasuries, Not for Japan The first US intervention in the yen in 28 years was officially a favor to an ally. The real calculation was to stop Japan from selling $1 trillion of US Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own cost of borrowing. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle The Hidden Risk in the US-Japan Yen Rescue US Treasuries Japanese yen FX intervention US Treasury Interest rates Carry trade carry trade forward premium puzzle Cakeism Treasury Convenience Yield\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-patrickboyle-美国救日元不是为日本-是为自家万亿美债/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/42184536/48d3d010465c2cda.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">31:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>America Rescued the Yen for Its Own Trillion in Treasuries, Not for Japan</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The first US intervention in the yen in 28 years was officially a favor to an ally. The real calculation was to stop Japan from selling $1 trillion of US Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own cost of borrowing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">US Treasuries</span><span class=\"tag\">Japanese yen</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The Order Calls Vaccines Soda and Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie Every sentence in the ‘gold standard’ executive order gets called a lie: splitting MMR to add needles, vaccines as bottled soda, Merck refusing outright — and the new CDC director will have to pick a side. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1348: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Vaccine policy MMR Outbreak data Parasites Long COVID Wastewater surveillance MMR / measles-mumps-rubella vaccine ACIP / Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices lyophilized PICO / the PICO question framework sterile insect technique RIG / rabies immune globulin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-twiv-行政令里的谎言-拆mmr与汽水比喻都是伪科学/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">55:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>The Order Calls Vaccines Soda and Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Every sentence in the ‘gold standard’ executive order gets called a lie: splitting MMR to add needles, vaccines as bottled soda, Merck refusing outright — and the new CDC director will have to pick a side.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Vaccine policy</span><span class=\"tag\">MMR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"The cure for picky-eating anxiety: no judgment, no rewards, dessert is just another food A child&#x27;s relationship with food does not hinge on whether they ate any particular thing. It hinges on whether the parent sorts food into good and bad, whether dessert gets used as a reward, and whether the parent gives themselves permission to feed according to what the child actually needs. The earlier picky-eating signals are recognized, the easier they are to change. Raising Good Humans Raising Good Humans Picky Eating &amp; Food Guilt with Jennifer Anderson Child feeding Picky eating Food anxiety Parent-child communication Body image Feeding psychology embodied independence hyper-palatable foods PSAE\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-raisinggh-挑食焦虑的解药-不评判-不奖励-甜点也是普通食物/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/216d7bb0-95d0-11f1-b9ad-6f2d14c4eade/image/6786871cff0ea61c3f706ebdda40515e.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"R\"><span class=\"dur\">46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Raising Good Humans</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>The cure for picky-eating anxiety: no judgment, no rewards, dessert is just another food</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A child&#x27;s relationship with food does not hinge on whether they ate any particular thing. It hinges on whether the parent sorts food into good and bad, whether dessert gets used as a reward, and whether the parent gives themselves permission to feed according to what the child actually needs. The earlier picky-eating signals are recognized, the easier they are to change.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Child feeding</span><span class=\"tag\">Picky eating</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political rollback and economic dependence Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both genuine feeling and performance, sitting on top of political rollback, economic dependence, and a reality that social media amplifies. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area Why straight dating feels bleak Heteropessimism Gender politics Dating culture Women&#x27;s bind Social commentary heteropessimism hopeful pessimism\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-grayarea-异性恋悲观主义-直女困境的真实与表演/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/a2ed43cc-fe19-11f0-8400-b7049bc68c1c/image/09d3576515488959f432d219d5c7416b.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">57:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political rollback and economic dependence</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both genuine feeling and performance, sitting on top of political rollback, economic dependence, and a reality that social media amplifies.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Heteropessimism</span><span class=\"tag\">Gender politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"El Niño Isn&#x27;t a Short-Term Shock, It&#x27;s a Permanent Loss of Growth El Niño is not just a passing weather shock: research shows it permanently depresses the path of economic growth, a single strong event can cost trillions of dollars within five years, and we have not adapted to it. Odd Lots Odd Lots A Historic El Niño Is Coming That Could Cost the World Trillions El Niño Climate economics Economic growth Global warming Adaptation strategy ENSO / El Niño-Southern Oscillation Teleconnection RONI / Relative Oceanic Niño Index Level effect\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-oddlots-厄尔尼诺不是短期冲击-而是永久性增长损失/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>El Niño Isn&#x27;t a Short-Term Shock, It&#x27;s a Permanent Loss of Growth</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">El Niño is not just a passing weather shock: research shows it permanently depresses the path of economic growth, a single strong event can cost trillions of dollars within five years, and we have not adapted to it.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">El Niño</span><span class=\"tag\">Climate economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Lindy Runs Entirely on DeepSeek; Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned Flo Crivello says the driver of Lindy&#x27;s whole agent stack is now DeepSeek — while he simultaneously argues the entire industry should be banned from using it, because competitors will use it and so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather see that prisoner&#x27;s dilemma solved by coordination. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution Lindy Teammate: Flo Crivello on Multiplayer Agents, Memory &amp; Why He&#x27;d Ban the Chinese Models He Uses Agent memory Context engineering Inference cost Chinese models Enterprise sales Prompt optimization hydration context bucket centary tree TOON hypothesis driven retrieval per-user LoRA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-cogrev-lindy-全线跑在-deepseek-上-创始人主张封禁中国模型/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/67f4c75e-93d8-11f1-bc73-4b7840ced6dd/image/4b0b55cbbf397c80de476a6b6e5e6d36.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:06:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Lindy Runs Entirely on DeepSeek; Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Flo Crivello says the driver of Lindy&#x27;s whole agent stack is now DeepSeek — while he simultaneously argues the entire industry should be banned from using it, because competitors will use it and so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather see that prisoner&#x27;s dilemma solved by coordination.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>12</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent memory</span><span class=\"tag\">Context engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"SK hynix&#x27;s turnaround ran on customer relationships, not on HBM technology SK hynix&#x27;s comeback was not a bet on HBM as a technology but a bet on customer relationships and sustained investment; Samsung, betting on PIM for edge inference, happened to hand its rival the sole-supplier position at the ChatGPT moment. Asianometry Asianometry SK hynix and the HBM Revolution Semiconductors HBM Memory chips Korean chaebol Advanced packaging AI compute HBM / High Bandwidth Memory TSV / Through Silicon Via TC-NCF / Thermal Compression with Non-Conductive Film MR-MUF / Mass Reflow Molded Underfill HBM-PIM / Processing-in-Memory ADR / American Depositary Receipt\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-asianometry-sk-hynix-靠-hbm-翻身-客户战略赢过周期/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/Cg5tAujp6Go/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">