never seen — all of it resting on using prompts to tame low-quality, heterogeneous data. The bottleneck is shifting to reliability, speed and physical distribution.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Robot models</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Did a Substation Wreck the 49ers? The Dose Is 40x Too Low, and the Data Says No The conspiracy theory that electromagnetic radiation from a substation caused the 49ers&#x27; injury wave gets dismantled point by point by radiation experts and injury databases: the dose is far below the safety threshold, the cited papers don&#x27;t hold up, the 2014 expansion was a different substation, and the data doesn&#x27;t show the 49ers are the worst off. Science Vs Science Vs We Solve the 49ers Viral Conspiracy Theory NFL Injury data EMF radiation Conspiracy theories Fact-checking Oxidative stress milligauss deep story\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-sciencevs-变电站不背这口锅-49人队伤病阴谋论被拆穿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/f521b120-2c30-11e6-b5f3-63ee984ee1a4/image/e7470287efbfa0aff068175bb6c31805.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Did a Substation Wreck the 49ers? The Dose Is 40x Too Low, and the Data Says No</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The conspiracy theory that electromagnetic radiation from a substation caused the 49ers&#x27; injury wave gets dismantled point by point by radiation experts and injury databases: the dose is far below the safety threshold, the cited papers don&#x27;t hold up, the 2014 expansion was a different substation, and the data doesn&#x27;t show the 49ers are the worst off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">NFL</span><span class=\"tag\">Injury data</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Coffee doesn&#x27;t get you drunk, and that is exactly why it produced the modern commercial intelligence network Coffee first supplied wakefulness for Sufi prayer; because it left drinkers sober rather than drunk, it left them talking, and the coffeehouse became an exchange for commercial intelligence, then reshaped the global economy through slave plantations and branding. Today&#x27;s arguments about the latte are still written into these five hundred years of history. In Our Time In Our Time Archive: Coffee Coffee Business history Colonialism Social networks Supply chains Italian coffee Sufis Levant Company Lloyd&#x27;s List Robusta Moka pot espresso\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-inourtime-咖啡因催生了近代商业情报网络与社交空间/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0m1q0p7.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">56:52</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Coffee doesn&#x27;t get you drunk, and that is exactly why it produced the modern commercial intelligence network</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Coffee first supplied wakefulness for Sufi prayer; because it left drinkers sober rather than drunk, it left them talking, and the coffeehouse became an exchange for commercial intelligence, then reshaped the global economy through slave plantations and branding. Today&#x27;s arguments about the latte are still written into these five hundred years of history.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>10</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Coffee</span><span class=\"tag\">Business history</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Female Testosterone Falls 1% a Year, Brain Metabolism 20% in Perimenopause Women should establish a hormone baseline in their twenties, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; brain glucose metabolism drops 20% on average in perimenopause, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance. Huberman Lab Huberman Lab Essentials: How to Optimize Female Hormone Health for Vitality &amp; Longevity | Dr. Sara Gottfried Female Hormones Testosterone Perimenopause Oral Contraceptives Brain Metabolism Continuous Glucose Monitoring SHBG / sex hormone-binding globulin CGM / continuous glucose monitor PCOS / polycystic ovary syndrome FDG PET / fluorodeoxyglucose positron emission tomography HPA axis / hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis CAC / coronary artery calcium score\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-huberman-女性激素真相-睾酮流失与围绝经期脑代谢/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/d5bc4646-96ca-11f1-aaf8-2bcc5308b57c/image/c939ff80ce31857dd7c3855498b342f4.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">38:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Huberman Lab</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Female Testosterone Falls 1% a Year, Brain Metabolism 20% in Perimenopause</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Women should establish a hormone baseline in their twenties, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; brain glucose metabolism drops 20% on average in perimenopause, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Female Hormones</span><span class=\"tag\">Testosterone</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The trucking rate spike is enforcement cutting supply, not demand returning English language proficiency enforcement, a crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability pulled capacity out at the same time. What ended a three-year trough was not freight volume coming back but a structural rise in the barrier to entry — so the next demand surge will hit a market that can no longer add supply the way it did during COVID. Odd Lots Odd Lots Trucking Is Booming Again, And Drivers Aren&#x27;t Happy About It Trucking Regulation Supply contraction Cyclical stocks Physical infrastructure Labor non-domiciled CDL ELD (electronic logging device) freight broker FMCSA safety rating spot vs contract rate owner operator\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-oddlots-这轮卡车运价上涨来自供给被砍-不是需求回来了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>The trucking rate spike is enforcement cutting supply, not demand returning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">English language proficiency enforcement, a crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability pulled capacity out at the same time. What ended a three-year trough was not freight volume coming back but a structural rise in the barrier to entry — so the next demand surge will hit a market that can no longer add supply the way it did during COVID.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trucking</span><span class=\"tag\">Regulation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"After Tupperware fired its queen, the company buried her book Brownie Wise turned Tupperware into an American household brand by selling it through housewives&#x27; living-room parties, then was fired for outshining the inventor, had the record of her life destroyed, and got no official recognition until a park was named for her in 2016. Throughline Throughline The blatant betrayal that erased the Tupperware queen from history Sales Revolution Women at Work Brand History American Business Organizational Power subversive domesticity burp Wonder Bowl Jubilee\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-throughline-特百惠女王遭公然背叛-被美国历史抹去/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2284x2284+0+0/resize/3000/quality/66/format/jpg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb6%2F91%2F1d82ed1b4fa4aaeed16a31e71f13%2F706a4af3-0aec-4384-baac-5304e54f98e0.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">49:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>After Tupperware fired its queen, the company buried her book</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Brownie Wise turned Tupperware into an American household brand by selling it through housewives&#x27; living-room parties, then was fired for outshining the inventor, had the record of her life destroyed, and got no official recognition until a park was named for her in 2016.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Sales Revolution</span><span class=\"tag\">Women at Work</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"LLMs industrialize the con, and single sign-on becomes the master switch When faking a job interview, monitoring an inbox and synthesizing a voice all cost close to nothing, anyone&#x27;s SSO account can be taken over silently; who the bank makes absorb the loss matters more than teaching users to spot phishing. Complex Systems Complex Systems LLMs and the economics of Evil, Inc., with Manish Goregaokar LLMs Anti-fraud Money laundering Cybersecurity Social engineering Supply chain attacks BEC (business email compromise) money mule AML (anti-money laundering) Regulation E desk name supply chain attack\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-complexsys-大模型把骗局工业化-单点登录成了总开关/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/6GtSkXQHQ068L7pFuoWXCujz5w4ulG2fYXCZhkptj1A/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS9hZTYx/MDE0ZTljZDc1NTZk/OTM1NWJkZDdiNjM5/Zjk0YS5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>LLMs industrialize the con, and single sign-on becomes the master switch</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">When faking a job interview, monitoring an inbox and synthesizing a voice all cost close to nothing, anyone&#x27;s SSO account can be taken over silently; who the bank makes absorb the loss matters more than teaching users to spot phishing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">LLMs</span><span class=\"tag\">Anti-fraud</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Romans knew the founding myth was false and used it as a diplomatic tool Rome&#x27;s origin myths were not history carved in stone but an elastic narrative Romans used to negotiate, to absorb other peoples, and to digest civil war; the archaeology even contradicts the 753 BC founding date outright. The Ancients The Ancients Romulus &amp; Remus Roman history Political mythology Archaeology Aeneas Romulus Oral tradition Rex Pomerium Casa Romuli Lupa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-ancients-罗马人清楚建城神话是虚构的-但照样当外交工具/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f9e74b795a6299fd3b58/1786360459782-d4158422-9610-4d6e-9464-82ce00eea17a.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">59:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Romans knew the founding myth was false and used it as a diplomatic tool</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Rome&#x27;s origin myths were not history carved in stone but an elastic narrative Romans used to negotiate, to absorb other peoples, and to digest civil war; the archaeology even contradicts the 753 BC founding date outright.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Roman history</span><span class=\"tag\">Political mythology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Elizabeth wanted Mary assassinated, but was forced to sign the death warrant Elizabeth I did not want Mary executed in public; she hoped someone would kill her privately under the Bond of Association. The Privy Council insisted on legal process, and in the end, even after the Queen had signed, they defied her wishes and rushed the warrant through the night to Fotheringhay. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 696. Elizabeth I vs The Catholics: Killing the Queen of Scots (Part 6) Elizabeth I Mary Stuart British history Intelligence war Cryptography Death penalty politics Bond of Association Act for the Queen&#x27;s Safety presence chamber Star Chamber cipher\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-12-restishistory-玛丽之死背后的真博弈-伊丽莎白想要暗杀-不想签字/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/00c0a118-2426-11ee-b258-73d331d0123b/image/db3295fcd9d3a7113e8000e931f0541d.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:09:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0812</span></div>\n<h2>Elizabeth wanted Mary assassinated, but was forced to sign the death warrant</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Elizabeth I did not want Mary executed in public; she hoped someone would kill her privately under the Bond of Association. The Privy Council insisted on legal process, and in the end, even after the Queen had signed, they defied her wishes and rushed the warrant through the night to Fotheringhay.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Elizabeth I</span><span class=\"tag\">Mary Stuart</span>\n</div></div></a>"]
