["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Female Testosterone Falls 1% a Year, Brain Metabolism 20% in Perimenopause Women should establish a hormone baseline in their twenties, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; brain glucose metabolism drops 20% on average in perimenopause, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance. Huberman Lab Huberman Lab Essentials: How to Optimize Female Hormone Health for Vitality &amp; Longevity | Dr. Sara Gottfried Female Hormones Testosterone Perimenopause Oral Contraceptives Brain Metabolism Continuous Glucose Monitoring SHBG / sex hormone-binding globulin CGM / continuous glucose monitor PCOS / polycystic ovary syndrome FDG PET / fluorodeoxyglucose positron emission tomography HPA axis / hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis CAC / coronary artery calcium score\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-huberman-女性激素真相-睾酮流失与围绝经期脑代谢/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a1ac1c82ed5e5947-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">38:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Huberman Lab</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Female Testosterone Falls 1% a Year, Brain Metabolism 20% in Perimenopause</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Women should establish a hormone baseline in their twenties, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; brain glucose metabolism drops 20% on average in perimenopause, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Female Hormones</span><span class=\"tag\">Testosterone</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The trucking rate spike is enforcement cutting supply, not demand returning English language proficiency enforcement, a crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability pulled capacity out at the same time. What ended a three-year trough was not freight volume coming back but a structural rise in the barrier to entry — so the next demand surge will hit a market that can no longer add supply the way it did during COVID. Odd Lots Odd Lots Trucking Is Booming Again, And Drivers Aren&#x27;t Happy About It Trucking Regulation Supply contraction Cyclical stocks Physical infrastructure Labor non-domiciled CDL ELD (electronic logging device) freight broker FMCSA safety rating spot vs contract rate owner operator\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-oddlots-这轮卡车运价上涨来自供给被砍-不是需求回来了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>The trucking rate spike is enforcement cutting supply, not demand returning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">English language proficiency enforcement, a crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability pulled capacity out at the same time. What ended a three-year trough was not freight volume coming back but a structural rise in the barrier to entry — so the next demand surge will hit a market that can no longer add supply the way it did during COVID.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trucking</span><span class=\"tag\">Regulation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"After Tupperware fired its queen, th